<!--
NODrugSL.DES - Defines sublingual absorption of NO in HumMod

Overview
This file models the pharmacokinetics of Nitric Oxide (NO) when administered sublingually.
It calculates absorption based on drug mass, membrane permeability, and bioavailability.

1. **Drug Concentration Calculation:** Determines drug concentration in the sublingual compartment.
2. **Absorption Dynamics:** Defines how much drug is lost from the sublingual space and absorbed into systemic circulation.
3. **First-Order Absorption:** Uses a permeability and bioavailability factor to simulate absorption kinetics.

How to Replicate for Another Drug
1. Change `<name> NODrugSL </name>` to `<name> NewDrugSL </name>`.
2. Adjust **BIOAVAIL** (fraction absorbed into circulation) and **PERM** (absorption rate) values.
3. Modify **SublingualVolume** based on the expected volume for the new drug.
4. Ensure that the **differential equation for Mass** correctly represents the drug’s absorption process.
5. Update `Loss` and `Change` formulas to fit the new drug’s absorption kinetics.

-->

HumMod / NODrugSL

Created : 25-Jul-13
Last Modified : 
Author : W Pruett
Copyright : 2006-2013
By : University Of Mississippi Medical Center
Schema : DES V1.0


 <structure><name> NODrugSL </name>

<variables>

<constant>
  <name> BIOAVAIL </name>
  <val> 0.4 </val> 
</constant>

<constant>
  <name> PERM </name> 
  <val> 0.1 </val> 
</constant>

<constant>
  <name> SublingualVolume(L) </name>
  <val> 0.001 </val> <!-- typically 0.2 to 1 mL --> 
</constant>

<var>
  <name> [NODrug] </name> 
</var>

<var>
  <name> Loss </name> 
</var>

</variables>

<equations>

<diffeq>
  <name> Mass </name>
  <integralname> Mass </integralname>
  <initialval> 0.0 </initialval> 
  <dervname> Change </dervname>
  <errorlim> 0.01 </errorlim> 
</diffeq>

</equations>

<definitions>

<block><name> CalcConc </name> 

<def>
  <name> [NODrug] </name>
  <val> Mass / SublingualVolume(L) </val> 
</def>

</block>

<block><name> Dervs </name> 

<def>
  <name> Loss </name>
  <val> BIOAVAIL * PERM * Mass  </val> 
</def>

<def>
  <name> Change </name>
  <val> - Loss / BIOAVAIL </val> 
</def>

</block>

</definitions>
</structure> 

End
